WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.919
Accurate labelling of blood culture bottles is essential to ensure correct identification and reliable results.

2
00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:11.531
Each bottle is labelled at the bedside immediately after collection.

3
00:00:11.531 --> 00:00:16.143
The label must include the patient's name and identification number.

4
00:00:16.143 --> 00:00:18.911
The date and time of collection.

5
00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:20.294
The collection site.

6
00:00:20.294 --> 00:00:22.139
And the collector's initials.

7
00:00:22.139 --> 00:00:27.674
Proper labelling prevents specimen errors and ensures traceability throughout the testing process.

